# Every packages/*/Dockerfile and gatekeepers/*/Dockerfile builds from the repo root as its
# context (`COPY . .` in each Dockerfile's own `build` stage — see e.g.
# packages/gatekeeper-base/Dockerfile's own header comment). Without this file, that `COPY . .`
# picks up everything below, including secrets and host-specific state, into the build stage's own
# image layer — even for files the final `runtime` stage never copies out of it, that layer is
# still cached locally and inspectable via `docker history`/the build cache (review lane 5, P3
# batch: "COPY . . without .dockerignore (.env into build cache layers)"). Mirrors .gitignore's own
# security-sensitive entries; the categories below it (build output, host data, editor/OS noise)
# are excluded because every image does its own `pnpm install`/`tsc` from a clean context, not
# because they are sensitive.

# --- secrets / environment (never let a real credential reach a build layer) -------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
docs/private/

# --- version control / editor / OS --------------------------------------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Claude Code local state (worktrees, session state — never build input) ---------------------
.claude/
.codegraph/

# --- reinstalled/rebuilt inside the image — a host copy would bloat the context and can mismatch
# the container's platform/arch (native deps) -----------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
**/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- host runtime data, never build input ---------------------------------------------------------
data/
sessions/
*.log

# --- local reference-only third-party source (excluded from the repo entirely, see .gitignore) ---
semantica-0.6.7/
cloudflare-os-main/
pi-0.84.4/
